

To generate the compat headers, the following files are required:

* compat.pl generates compat headers from annotations produced by clang-tidy
* clang-tidy needs a source file and compile_commands.json to reproduce the
  compilation steps
* scripts/clang-tools/gen_compile_commands.py creates compile_commands.json
  from .*.cmd files
* the .*.cmd files are created by Kbuild when a .c file is compiled
* regen64.c is a dummy C program that includes all possible uapi headers


These dependencies translate into steps for generating the compat headers.
Run the commands below from the top-level kernel source directory:

make ARCH=riscv LLVM=/path/to/llvm/bin/ \
    CC="clang -target riscv64-unknown-linux-gnu" \
    HOSTCC="clang -target x86_64" \
    compat/regen64.o

python3 scripts/clang-tools/gen_compile_commands.py \
    compat/ -o compat/compile_commands.json

clang-tidy --checks="-*,cheri-Uapi*" --header-filter=".*" -system-headers \
    compat/regen64.c > compat/clt.log

perl ./compat/compat.pl ./compat/clt.log
